  "summary": "On 8 July 1853 US Navy Commodore Matthew Perry led a squadron into Tokyo Bay, arriving at Uraga with a letter from the US President for the Japanese Emperor. He returned in 1854 with a larger squadron, and the Treaty of Kanagawa of 31 March 1854 opened Shimoda and Hakodate to US ships and provided for stranded American sailors.",
